    b_honeypot_long: `<p style="margin:0 0 8px;line-height:1.7;font-size:12px">This is a curiosity-driven experiment I set up to learn more about how attacks actually happen in practice. Using VirtualBox, I simulated a simple honeypot environment with two virtual machines - one running Kali Linux and the other Alpine Linux.</p><p style="margin:0 0 8px;line-height:1.7;font-size:12px">I am using Cowrie as the SSH honeypot, which logs all login attempts, commands executed by attackers, and full session activity. The whole setup is isolated, no real systems involved - just a hands-on way to observe and understand attack patterns in a safe environment.</p><p style="margin:0;line-height:1.7;font-size:12px;color:#555"><em>Status: ongoing - learning experiment.</em></p>`,
    
